Root cause — DSS/prepass ordering race in the frame pipeline:

  Frame N:
    1. dynamic-shadow-system.frameUpdate: bomber LTW changed → invalidateShadowMap() → needsUpdate=true.
    2. outline-prepass-system.frameUpdate: source bombers set visible=false, renderSceneToTarget() calls device.render().
       Three.js sees autoUpdate=false + needsUpdate=true → bakes shadow map with bombers hidden → needsUpdate=false.
    3. draw(): device.render() — main render.
       Three.js sees autoUpdate=false + needsUpdate=false → skips shadow update.
       Scene renders with shadow map from step 2 (no bomber shadows).

Affected files:
  engine/render/three-render-adapter.ts:1630-1637  renderSceneToTarget — no shadow-state guard
  engine/render/systems/dynamic-shadow-system.ts:165-177  sets autoUpdate=false + invalidates on movement
  engine/render/systems/outline-prepass-system.ts:170  renderSceneToTarget call site

Fix outline (one change in renderSceneToTarget):
  Save+clear shadow state before secondary render, restore after, so the prepass never consumes a pending needsUpdate token:
    const savedAutoUpdate = this.device.shadowMap.autoUpdate;
    const savedNeedsUpdate = this.device.shadowMap.needsUpdate;
    this.device.shadowMap.autoUpdate = false;
    this.device.shadowMap.needsUpdate = false;
    // ... render to target ...
    this.device.shadowMap.autoUpdate = savedAutoUpdate;
    this.device.shadowMap.needsUpdate = savedNeedsUpdate;
  Regression test: ShadowCaster{dynamic:true} bombers + outline prepass enabled → floor has non-zero shadow after first movement.
